Z||000007||stimpy||02-09-2001||10:26 AM||||No kidding. Here's my story. Today is my birthday (Happy Birthday stimpy. Thanks) and last night I watched hockey until 12. (0-0 tie). Then at midnight (officially my b-day) I go out into the den, which is a converted garage, to check up on the forum. My feet go squish-squish on the carpet. AAAGH! The water heater has taken a dump, flooding the whole room. When I attempt to turn the water off at the top, the valve won't shut. It turns, but water continues to run.<BR>So, I go out to the front yard, pull up the cover to the main shut-off, and it's filled with 2 feet of COLD muddy water. So I strip down to a t-shirt (and pants, you sickos) and kneel down it the squishy mud to reach my hand deep in the water. I just know there is gonna be a water moccasin in there). While this is going on, a cold front is moving in with 55 mph winds and sleet. Soon I'm being pelted with projectiles of garbage (it's trash day) being hurled from the knocked down garbage cans and recycle bins.<P>I'm really tempted to stay in bed today. ||||reg||8
